&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49907492</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:42:17 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Maverank, a free AI-readiness check for your website</title><link>https://maverank.com/tools/ai-visibility-checker</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi HN, I'm David. I build SaaS products and lately I've been a bit obsessed with whether ChatGPT recommends mine or a competitor's.&lt;p&gt;I built Maverank's free checker to find problems I could fix on my own sites. Things like blocked crawlers, content that only loads with JavaScript, or pages that don't explain what the product does.&lt;p&gt;Enter a URL and you'll get a score out of 100, a breakdown of the checks, and suggestions for what to fix. You don't need an account for the free check, but more checks are available through a 7-day trial.&lt;p&gt;Scoring 100 doesn't mean ChatGPT will recommend you. It's a way to spot problems that could make your site harder to read or understand.&lt;p&gt;After making changes, you can check again, share your score, or compare it with sites on the leaderboard.&lt;p&gt;I'd appreciate hearing what it finds on something you've built, especially if a check gets something wrong or suggests an unhelpful fix.&lt;/p&gt;
